**************************************************
* Starting Signal Variable Section of Model      *
**************************************************
*
*         idsv          isvn          ilcn          icn1          icn2
             1             0             0             0             0
* sv2: relief-valve control pressure. Sensed at the accumulator outlet, not
* at the cell adjacent to the valve seat: static pressure next to a choked
* seat collapses by the dynamic head (~MPa for near-sonic steam), which
* exceeds the 0.86 MPa deadband and chatters the valve. The reference's
* reclosure at 1.44 s during accumulator blowdown implies quasi-static
* sensing of the supply-side pressure.
*         idsv          isvn          ilcn          icn1          icn2
             2            21            30             2             0
**************************************************
* Finished Signal Variable Section of Model      *
**************************************************
*
***********************************
* Starting Trip Section of Model  *
***********************************
*
*         Trip Storage Count Card
*         ntse          ntct          ntsf          ntdp          ntsd
             0             0             0             0             0
*
*trip                    101
* Isolation valve closure at t = 1.0 s.
* isrt=2: OFF below setp(1), ON-forward above setp(2) -> vtb1 closes the valve.
*         idtp          isrt          iset          itst          idsg
           101             2             0             1             1
*      setp(1)       setp(2)
         0.999           1.0
*      dtsp(1)       dtsp(2)
           0.0           0.0
*      ifsp(1)       ifsp(2)
             0             0
*
*trip                    102
* Relief valve hysteresis on inlet pressure (pipe 40 cell 9).
* isrt=-3: ON-reverse (close, vtb2) below setp(1); OFF (hold) in the deadband;
* ON-forward (open, vtb1) above setp(4).
*         idtp          isrt          iset          itst          idsg
           102            -3             0             1             2
* setp(2) sits well above setp(1): once reclosure starts at 16.38 MPa, the
* closing valve throttles the line and pressure recovers ~0.2 MPa; a narrow
* band would cancel the stroke mid-close and strand the valve partially open.
* A real S/RV completes its spring-driven closure once it leaves the seat.
*      setp(1)       setp(2)       setp(3)       setp(4)
       16.38E6       16.90E6       17.23E6       17.24E6
*      dtsp(1)       dtsp(2)       dtsp(3)       dtsp(4)
           0.0           0.0           0.0           0.0
*      ifsp(1)       ifsp(2)       ifsp(3)       ifsp(4)
             0             0             0             0
*
***********************************
* Finished Trip Section of Model  *
